direction: down
title: |md
  # From application to credit score
| {near: top-center}

input: |md
  **Loan application**

  income, credit history, verification,

  loan amount, rate, purpose, credit profile
| {shape: rectangle; class: actor}
derive: |md
  **Derive loan burden**

  loan amount ÷ (income + 1)
| {shape: rectangle; class: box}
bin: |md
  **Assign attributes**

  numeric values fall into fitted bins;

  categories map directly
| {shape: rectangle; class: box}
woe: |md
  **Look up Weight of Evidence**

  ln(share of good ÷ share of bad) for each attribute
| {shape: rectangle; class: box}
model: |md
  **Logistic regression**

  ln(odds of default) = intercept + Σ coefficient × WOE
| {shape: rectangle; class: key}
pd: |md
  **Probability of default**

  1 ÷ (1 + e^(−ln odds))

  example: 5.4%
| {shape: rectangle; class: good}
score: |md
  **Credit score**

  Offset − Factor × ln(odds)

  600 points at 50:1 odds, 20 points double the odds

  example: 569.55
| {shape: rectangle; class: good}
points: |md
  **Score attribution**

  base 562 + points per characteristic,

  each −Factor × coefficient × WOE
| {shape: rectangle; class: good}
grade: |md
  **Risk grade**

  AAA to C by score band

  example: BB
| {shape: rectangle; class: good}
input -> derive
derive -> bin
bin -> woe
woe -> model
model -> pd
model -> score
model -> points
score -> grade
